; The consciousness class-surface ternary port's conformance world (issue
; #588, ADR204 W10, Task 1) — the measured-ternary declaration surface for
; `consciousness.bsl`, plus the seed world its rules run against.
;
; FIRST `probability`-LANE CONSUMER, pinned by name: no committed .bscn
; declared a `probability` deffield before this file (archaeology digest
; B.2, ai/scratch/2026-08-15-class-surface-port-archaeology.md — every
; [0,1] value before rode `int`, raw or x1e6-scaled, territory precedent).
; social-class/revolutionary|liberal|fascist below are that lane's mint.
;
; UNPOSITIONED IDIOM (the port's absence posture, L-ABS): ternary fields
; are NEVER defaulted into existence. A never-positioned class carries no
; r/l/f and no dominant-worldview; reads error loud (III.11,
; scenario.rs's own "No defaults" contract). Rules optional-bind with
; declared `0.0p` defaults and gate on the sum: zero IS "no reading"
; (a positioned class is a simplex point — its shares sum to 1, so a zero
; sum is exactly never-positioned, by construction, not by epsilon).
;
; REUSE CHECK (carrier qnames): `social-class/value-produced` is verbatim
; from two-classes.bscn (`int extensive`). `social-class/population`,
; `social-class/wealth`, `social-class/active` match
; production-conformance.bscn's spellings — with one deliberate KIND
; divergence: the two `active` latches here are declared `intensive`
; (a 0/1 latch is a per-node state, never a summed quantity; production-
; conformance.bscn and organization-foundation.bscn declare the same
; qnames `extensive` — deffield kinds are scenario-local registries, so
; this is a recorded divergence, not a collision, and no fold in this
; pack ever sums a latch). `social-class/wages-paid` is NEW — the frozen
; `w_paid` (ideology.py:239), deliberately NOT two-classes.bscn's
; `social-class/wages` (that fixture's own name for the fundamental-
; theorem read, not the ideology system's wage field).
; `organization/active` follows the production.bsl-header item-2 latch
; convention (no bool on the live .bscn path).
;
; THE FOUR SPELLING-SPIKE VERDICTS (Task 1's chartered discoveries):
;
;   1. PROBABILITY-LANE LITERALS — `0.0p` / `1.0p` (and any p-suffixed
;      unit-interval literal) are LAWFUL: docs/reference/bsl.ebnf's
;      `scaled-lit` admits suffixes "$" | "p" | "i" | "c" | "r", and
;      reader.rs's classify_unit_interval bounds them to scale <= 9 and
;      value in [0,1] (E-LEX-023 / E-LEX-024). Kind-blind at every door:
;      node field-init into a probability/intensity/coefficient field
;      accepts int or p/i/c literals (scenario.rs's
;      attribute_value_unit_interval, mirroring structural_verbs.rs's
;      store_range_check one call frame later); edge strengths likewise
;      (load_edge, verdict 3). The frozen _EPSILON = 1e-10
;      (consciousness_routing.py:41) is INEXPRESSIBLE as a p/i/c literal
;      (E-LEX-023, scale <= 9) — controller ruling 4 resolves it: the
;      consuming rule (Task 3) binds epsilon as the expr quotient
;      `(/ 1c 10000000000)`, bit-identical to Python's 1e-10 via one
;      correctly-rounded IEEE-754 division, so NO defconst row for it
;      exists here at all.
;
;   2. DEFENUM SHARING ACROSS SCENARIO FILES — NOT SERVED. load_scenario
;      admits exactly ONE (scenario ...) form per source (scenario.rs's
;      own top-level cardinality check), and run_once / run_once_into /
;      TickSession each take ONE scenario string, so this file RE-DECLARES
;      (defenum WorldView (REVOLUTIONARY LIBERAL FASCIST)) below rather
;      than loading worldview-foundation.bscn's registry alongside. The
;      ruled member order (declaration order IS the storage ordinal,
;      ADR195) is pinned for this re-declaration by
;      tick_goldens.rs's
;      consciousness_ternary_worldview_member_order_is_the_ruled_ordinal,
;      mirroring the mint's own registry assertion.
;      RETIRED by Train B item 4 (#591, D157, 2026-08-17): served now, via
;      a DECLARATION PRELUDE, not scenario-to-scenario sharing —
;      load_scenario_with_prelude reads content/declarations/worldview.bscn
;      first (declaration forms only, no (scenario ...) wrapper, so the
;      one-form-per-source cardinality check above is untouched) and
;      threads its registries into this scenario's own load.
;      EnumRegistry::declare's new identical-recognition arm (same train)
;      is what makes this compatible with a re-declaration, though this
;      file no longer re-declares: the (defenum WorldView ...) form below
;      is DELETED, and the deffield at social-class/dominant-worldview
;      resolves against the prelude's registry directly.
;      consciousness_ternary_worldview_member_order_is_the_ruled_ordinal is
;      a declared test death (tick_goldens.rs) — the re-declaration it
;      guarded no longer exists; the mint's own
;      worldview_member_order_is_the_ruled_ordinal is the single surviving
;      ordinal guard, over a byte-identical defenum line.
;
;   3. EDGE DECLARATION + EDGE-ATTRIBUTE DEFFIELD SYNTAX — edges seed as
;      (edge EdgeType/<MEMBER> <from> <to> <strength>) where strength is
;      an int or a p/i/c unit-interval literal, kind-blind (load_edge;
;      the SOLIDARITY edges below carry 0.4p / 0.5p / 0.9p). Edge
;      attributes declare as (deffield <edge-type-lower>/<field> <type>
;      <kind>) — the `(deffield solidarity/tension intensity intensive)`
;      precedent, edge-write-lane-e2e.bscn (ADR203/ADR205). SCENARIO-SIDE
;      EDGE-ATTRIBUTE SEEDING IS NOT SERVED: load_edge pattern-matches
;      exactly (edge <enum-ref> <from> <to> <strength>), no attribute
;      pairs. Controller ruling 2 took the consequence: the frozen
;      engine's incoming-WAGES value_flow fold-sum (ideology.py:299-309)
;      narrows to ONE declared class-side flow value per class per tick —
;      `social-class/wages-received` below, exact for single-employer
;      content — so this world seeds NO WAGES edges and declares NO
;      edge-attribute deffield. The seeding gap itself is recorded for
;      the port train's closing ADR.
;      RETIRED by Train B item 3 (#591, D151's discharge, 2026-08-17):
;      scenario-side edge-attribute seeding IS now served — the
;      `(edge-attr ...)` form (D156) — and this world now seeds three
;      WAGES edges plus declares the `wages/value-flow` edge-attribute
;      deffield below; `social-class/wages-received` is gone.
;      The wage flow rides the pushed `social-class/wages-inbox`
;      accumulator (`consciousness/p2-wages-push`, consciousness.bsl)
;      instead of the declared class-side flow value this paragraph
;      originally recorded.
;
;   4. FLOAT-EXPR -> INT-FIELD WRITE COERCION — THERE IS NONE. The store
;      is kind-blind f64 end to end: structural_verbs.rs's
;      numeric_write_value stores a Value::Real verbatim into any
;      non-enum field, so production.bsl's `(add output)` into the
;      `int extensive` social-class/wealth lands NON-INTEGRAL values
;      (production_conformance.rs pins worker-pp wealth
;      11.538461538461538 bit-for-bit). Controller ruling 3's rounding
;      D-row, verbatim: "no implicit truncation at the store; the int
;      lane holds verbatim f64; `floor` is the content-explicit
;      truncation intrinsic, unused in this pack."
;      RETIRED by Train B item 6 (`BslType::Real`): the fields this row governed now declare `real`; the store law itself (verbatim f64, no implicit truncation, `floor` available) is unchanged — only the declared home moved.
;
;      FIX-ROUND DISCOVERY (ruling 3's escape clause, exercised), then
;      FIX-ROUND-2 CORRECTION (the escape retired): the FULL seed/write
;      law for the int lane, mapped across the two rounds —
;        * fractional WRITES into int-typed fields are stored VERBATIM
;          (numeric_write_value; production-conformance's pinned
;          11.538461538461538) — no coercion, no rounding;
;        * fractional SEEDS into int-typed fields are REFUSED by the
;          loader — scenario.rs's attribute_value_int accepts ONLY
;          integer literals, captured verbatim:
;            "node `class-exploited` field `social-class/agitation`:
;             expected an integer literal, found Scaled(ScaledLit {
;             kind: Intensity, unscaled: 1, scale: 1 })"
;      Fix round 1 therefore tried the one lawful door for fractional
;      seeds and declared agitation `intensity intensive` (0.1i/0.2i).
;      Fix round 2 RETIRED that escape (controller ruling): the
;      unit-interval lane's E-EVAL-020 [0,1] ceiling is tick-fatal under
;      the frozen agitation domain [0,∞) (social_class.py:95-102, "Raw
;      political energy from crisis [0.0, inf)") — Task 3's class-bribed
;      vector writes 1.0 undecayed in its first tick (zero seed + the
;      1.0 rent component) and the accumulator crosses the ceiling at
;      tick 2 (0.9 decayed + 1.0 fresh = 1.9). So agitation is
;      `int intensive` (the verbatim-f64 lane) and the seeds are 0:
;      agitation is a PRODUCED accumulator (R-MEASURED) — content seeds
;      it at zero and Task 3's vectors produce it; the fractional
;      increments then land as rule writes, where the verbatim lane is
;      lawful. wage-balance (signed) and solidarity-inbox (sums can
;      exceed 1.0) were never unit-interval candidates
;      (store_range_check refuses out-of-[0,1] unit-interval values) —
;      they stay int-typed, verbatim-f64, and unseeded here (later
;      tasks write them).
;
; Node census, in declaration order (which fixes the store ids):
;   0  class-exploited    positioned (0.5, 0.4, 0.1), anchored, wage cut
;                         this tick (previous-wages 10 -> wages-inbox 9),
;                         one org SOLIDARITY edge (0.4p) — later tasks'
;                         revolutionary-routing vector.
;   1  class-bribed       positioned (0.1, 0.6, 0.3), positive wage balance
;                         (12 received vs 10 produced), NO org solidarity —
;                         later tasks' ADR016 fascist-routing vector; its
;                         outgoing SOLIDARITY 0.9p to class-emergent is
;                         gate-BLOCKED (its r = 0.1 <= the 0.3 activation
;                         threshold): the percolation fail arm.
;   2  class-unpositioned NO anchors, NO ternary — the UNPOSITIONED
;                         witness: p0's guard rejects it (sentinel -1),
;                         every ternary read errors absent.
;   3  class-emergent     anchors, NO ternary — p0 positions it at the
;                         ruled rest state (0, 1, 0) THIS tick; the whole
;                         later pipeline runs on it same-tick (D116).
;                         dominant-worldview is written by p8 same-tick —
;                         the measured readout LIBERAL — NEVER by p0: the
;                         one-home law (its ONLY writer is
;                         consciousness/p8-dominant-worldview, controller
;                         ruling 1; Task 1 pinned the absence, Task 2's
;                         handoff flipped the pin positive).
;   4  employer           active, population, NO anchors — the anchorless
;                         witness: never positioned (p0's anchor guard),
;                         never routed (the sum-guard).
;   5  org-solid          the org solidarity source (active latch).
;
; Task-2 read-path fixtures (consciousness/p8-dominant-worldview's tie
; vectors): the tv classes seed ONLY population, active=1, the ternary, and
; agitation 0 — NO anchors, NO edges — so Task 3's update rules never touch
; them (p1's inbox-reset will — a harmless machinery write, hash-covered).
; Expected dominants under the frozen tie-break (argmax, then the ruled order
; LIBERAL > REVOLUTIONARY > FASCIST within a STRICT 1e-6 of the max,
; consciousness.py:177-192):
;   6  tv-liberal-clear    (0.2, 0.5, 0.3) -> LIBERAL      (clear l max)
;   7  tv-revolutionary-clear (0.6, 0.4, 0.0) -> REVOLUTIONARY (clear r max)
;   8  tv-fascist-clear    (0.2, 0.3, 0.5) -> FASCIST      (clear f max)
;   9  tv-tie-lr           (0.5, 0.5, 0.0) -> LIBERAL      (l == r at max: L > R)
;  10  tv-tie-rf           (0.5, 0.0, 0.5) -> REVOLUTIONARY (r == f at max: R > F)
;  11  tv-tie-lf           (0.0, 0.5, 0.5) -> LIBERAL      (l == f at max: L > F)
;  12  tv-strict-gap       (0.333333, 0.333333, 0.333334) -> FASCIST — the
;                         STRICTNESS witness: the literal gap is 1e-6 in
;                         decimal, and the frozen law's strict `<` excludes
;                         the boundary — decimal-exact (1e-6 < 1e-6 is
;                         false) and f64-verbatim agree (dl = mx - l =
;                         1.00000000002875566e-06 > fl(1e-6) =
;                         9.99999999999999955e-07, so neither runner-up
;                         qualifies and the unique max wins; frozen ground
;                         truth dominant_tendency returns fascist — controller
;                         ruling 2026-08-15, Task-2 NEEDS_CONTEXT).
;  13  tv-tie-all-true     (0.333333, 0.333333, 0.333333) -> LIBERAL — the
;                         TRUE all-equal tie-order witness (dl = 0 < 1e-6, so
;                         LIBERAL takes the ruled order's first slot). Its
;                         0.999999 sum is content-visible and lawful: the
;                         store checks per-field ranges only, no store-side
;                         simplex enforcement — p6-route's closure remainder
;                         branch would heal it toward liberal if it ever
;                         routed (A-001 again).
;
; Small ints by design — increments stay order-1 so the exact-f64 anchors
; are hand-checkable.
(scenario consciousness/ternary-conformance
  (defvocabulary NodeType (SOCIAL_CLASS ORGANIZATION))
  (defvocabulary EdgeType (SOLIDARITY WAGES))

  ; ---- carriers (reuse exact qnames from two-classes.bscn where present) ----
  (deffield social-class/population int extensive)
  (deffield social-class/active int intensive)            ; 0/1 latch convention (no bool on the live path)
  (deffield social-class/wealth real extensive)
  (deffield social-class/wages-paid int extensive)        ; frozen w_paid (ideology.py:239)
  (deffield social-class/value-produced int extensive)    ; frozen v_produced (ideology.py:240)
  (deffield organization/active int intensive)            ; latch convention (production.bsl header item 2)

  ; ---- the ternary surface (FIRST probability deffields in committed content) ----
  (deffield social-class/revolutionary probability intensive)
  (deffield social-class/liberal probability intensive)
  (deffield social-class/fascist probability intensive)
  (deffield social-class/dominant-worldview enum WorldView)   ; consumes the WorldView declaration from content/declarations/worldview.bscn via the prelude (Train B item 4, #591, D157) — no re-declaration; ONLY Task 2's consciousness/p8-dominant-worldview writes it (one-home law, controller ruling 1)

  ; ---- update-law machinery (verbatim-f64 posture: no store coercion, spike 4) ----
  (deffield social-class/agitation real intensive)         ; [0,∞) raw f64 (frozen: ge=0.0, unbounded — social_class.py:95-102). Retired from the verbatim-f64 int lane by Train B item 6 (the real type); zero seeds remain (R-MEASURED: produced, never authored)
  (deffield social-class/wage-balance real intensive)      ; [-1,1] SIGNED raw f64 — a unit-interval type would refuse the negative half (store_range_check)
  (deffield social-class/solidarity-inbox real intensive)  ; [0,n) strength-sum raw f64 — can exceed 1.0, so no unit-interval type is lawful; reset per tick (later tasks)
  (deffield wages/value-flow real intensive)               ; the per-edge wage flow (ADR203 edge deffield; retired-then-restored: W10's D151 narrowing discharged by Train B item 3)
  (deffield social-class/wages-inbox real intensive)       ; [0,n) flow-sum — the push-over-pull accumulator (D136): reset by p1, pushed by p2-wages-push, read by p5, persisted by p7
  (deffield social-class/repression-faced intensity intensive) ; declared input only; nothing in Rust writes it yet
  (deffield social-class/previous-wages real intensive)    ; raw units (the persistent_data re-home, digest gap 4)
  (deffield social-class/previous-wealth real intensive)

  ; ---- defines environment (transcribed; line cites = src/babylon/data/defines.yaml) ----
  (defconst consciousness/routing-scale 0.2c)                    ; :213
  (defconst consciousness/agitation-decay-rate 0.1c)             ; :214
  (defconst consciousness/exploitation-sensitivity 0.15c)        ; :215
  (defconst consciousness/rent-decline-sensitivity 0.2c)         ; :216
  (defconst consciousness/reproduction-visibility-coefficient 0.1c) ; :217 — term is 0.0 verbatim (ideology.py:375)
  (defconst consciousness/agitation-consumption-rate 0.6c)       ; :220
  (defconst consciousness/chauvinist-pressure-scale 1.0c)        ; :228
  (defconst consciousness/repression-level-sensitivity 0.02c)    ; :229
  (defconst consciousness/default-repression-faced 0.5c)         ; :167 (default_repression; DEFAULT_REPRESSION_FACED's alias target, 0.5, verified against defines.yaml at execution)
  (defconst consciousness/solidarity-activation-threshold 0.3c)  ; :184 (activation_threshold)
  (defconst consciousness/negligible-transmission 0.01c)         ; :186
  (defconst consciousness/wage-deterioration-stub 0.0c)          ; D-row: opposition_states graph attr has no BSL surface
  (defconst consciousness/popular-front-suppression-stub 0.0c)   ; D-row: electoral register absent (exact under register-absent content, ideology.py:401-409)

  ; class-exploited — positioned, anchored, wage cut this tick, one org
  ; SOLIDARITY edge (strength 0.4p): the revolutionary-routing vector.
  (node class-exploited NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 1000) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 50) (social-class/wages-paid 9) (social-class/value-produced 10)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.5p) (social-class/liberal 0.4p) (social-class/fascist 0.1p)
    (social-class/agitation 0)                         ; produced accumulator (R-MEASURED): zero-seeded, Task 3 produces it
    (social-class/previous-wages 10)
    (social-class/previous-wealth 50))

  ; class-bribed — positioned, positive balance (12/10 -> +0.0909…), NO
  ; solidarity: the ADR016 fascist-routing vector; wealth declines 95 -> 90
  ; (the rent component). Also its outgoing SOLIDARITY 0.9p to class-emergent
  ; is gate-BLOCKED (its r = 0.1 <= 0.3): the percolation fail arm.
  (node class-bribed NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 800) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 90) (social-class/wages-paid 12) (social-class/value-produced 10)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.1p) (social-class/liberal 0.6p) (social-class/fascist 0.3p)
    (social-class/agitation 0)                         ; produced accumulator (R-MEASURED): zero-seeded, Task 3 produces it
    (social-class/previous-wages 12)
    (social-class/previous-wealth 95))

  ; class-unpositioned — NO anchors, NO ternary: the UNPOSITIONED witness.
  (node class-unpositioned NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 500) (social-class/active 1))

  ; class-emergent — anchors, NO ternary: p0 positions it at (0,1,0) this tick,
  ; then the whole pipeline runs on it same-tick (D116). Wage cut 9 -> 8 keeps
  ; its agitation live so the solidarity push lands on a routing class.
  (node class-emergent NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 600) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/wealth 30) (social-class/wages-paid 8) (social-class/value-produced 10)
    (social-class/previous-wages 9) (social-class/previous-wealth 30))

  ; employer — active, NO anchors: the anchorless witness that must never
  ; be positioned (p0 guard) nor routed (sum-guard).
  (node employer NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 50) (social-class/active 1))

  ; The wage flow, un-narrowed (D151 discharge, Train B item 3, #591):
  ; employer's per-class WAGES edges carry the seeded flow directly, pushed
  ; into each class's wages-inbox by consciousness/p2-wages-push. Strength
  ; 1.0c is a structural presence marker only — nothing reads WAGES
  ; strength (the register row).
  (edge EdgeType/WAGES employer class-exploited 1.0c)
  (edge-attr EdgeType/WAGES employer class-exploited wages/value-flow 9)
  (edge EdgeType/WAGES employer class-bribed 1.0c)
  (edge-attr EdgeType/WAGES employer class-bribed wages/value-flow 12)
  (edge EdgeType/WAGES employer class-emergent 1.0c)
  (edge-attr EdgeType/WAGES employer class-emergent wages/value-flow 8)

  ; org-solid — the org solidarity source (active latch convention).
  (node org-solid NodeType/ORGANIZATION (organization/active 1))

  ; ---- Task 2 read-path fixtures (p8-dominant-worldview's tie vectors) ----
  ; Seed ONLY population / active=1 / the ternary / agitation 0 — NO anchors,
  ; NO edges, so Task 3's update rules never touch them. Expected dominants
  ; per the census table above.
  (node tv-liberal-clear NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.2p) (social-class/liberal 0.5p) (social-class/fascist 0.3p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  (node tv-revolutionary-clear NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.6p) (social-class/liberal 0.4p) (social-class/fascist 0.0p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  (node tv-fascist-clear NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.2p) (social-class/liberal 0.3p) (social-class/fascist 0.5p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  (node tv-tie-lr NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.5p) (social-class/liberal 0.5p) (social-class/fascist 0.0p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  (node tv-tie-rf NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.5p) (social-class/liberal 0.0p) (social-class/fascist 0.5p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  (node tv-tie-lf NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.0p) (social-class/liberal 0.5p) (social-class/fascist 0.5p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  ; STRICTNESS witness: a decimal-1e-6 gap is NOT a tie (strict `<` excludes
  ; the boundary; f64 lands the gap just ABOVE fl(1e-6)) — FASCIST.
  (node tv-strict-gap NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.333333p) (social-class/liberal 0.333333p) (social-class/fascist 0.333334p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))
  ; TRUE all-equal tie: ruled order's first slot — LIBERAL. Sum 0.999999 is
  ; lawful content (per-field store checks only; no store-side simplex law).
  (node tv-tie-all-true NodeType/SOCIAL_CLASS
    (social-class/population 100) (social-class/active 1)
    (social-class/revolutionary 0.333333p) (social-class/liberal 0.333333p) (social-class/fascist 0.333333p)
    (social-class/agitation 0))

  (edge EdgeType/SOLIDARITY org-solid class-exploited 0.4p)
  (edge EdgeType/SOLIDARITY class-exploited class-emergent 0.5p)
  (edge EdgeType/SOLIDARITY class-bribed class-emergent 0.9p))
